  </note>
  <heading level="2">Multiply a Trinomial by a Binomial</heading>
  <paragraph>We have multiplied monomials by monomials, monomials by polynomials, and binomials by binomials. Now we're ready to multiply a trinomial by a binomial. Remember, the FOIL method will not work in this case, but we can use either the Distributive Property or the Vertical Method. We first look at an example using the Distributive Property.</paragraph>
  <example number="10.43">
    <problem>
      <paragraph>Multiply using the Distributive Property: $$(x + 3)(2x^{2} - 5x + 8).$$</paragraph>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <cell/>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Distribute.</cell>
            <cell/>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Multiply.</cell>
            <cell>$$2x^{3} - 5x^{2} + 8x + 6x^{2} - 15x + 24$$</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Combine like terms.</cell>
            <cell>$$2x^{3} + x^{2} - 7x + 24$$</cell>
